From 6149abaf41a195ca48d60fe8accd5fed924874dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:13:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] backends/color: Shut down store work before manager
 resources disappear

When the color manager is disposed while color store or color device
work is still in flight (profile generation, ICC directory monitoring,
reading stored profiles, colord connection), the pending callbacks run
later against a manager, store or device that is already gone.

Add meta_color_store_shutdown(), called from the manager's dispose
before its resources are released and from the store's finalize. It
cancels the store's cancellable and stops the ICC directory monitor.
Every asynchronous step of the store and of device profile generation
now checks for cancellation first and returns a cancelled error instead
of touching its owner, and the store keeps a reference for the duration
of its own file reads. A request for a device profile made after
shutdown completes with a cancellation error. The colord callbacks of
the manager only cast their user data after the finish call has
reported success. A color profile keeps its own reference to the colord
client rather than reaching it through the manager, so it can still
delete its colord profile while being finalized late.

query_file_info_cb() reads the store's cancellable before handing its
reference to the load callback, rather than in the same call that
steals it, since the evaluation order of function arguments is
unspecified.

Link: TBD-MR
